+# Fourth pass (2026-10-04): A09 fix in the test builder, C-L04-6b
+
+## 22. A09 (`lastBoardRefreshAt`) is fixed in the test builder; `refreshBoard()` is rejected before 30 days with the expected message; `syncBoard()` stays the separate exit path; a negative control shows the test detects the old defect
+
+**Classification:** measurement (fix of a test-tool gap; no contract or policy change). Resolves item 19.
+- **Fix:** `testonly-build-one-v5.js` and `testonly-build-one.js` write `ValidatorsBoard.lastBoardRefreshAt` (slot 7) = the genesis timestamp when the board is seeded. The pre-fix files are kept as `*.pre-A09-fix`; `BUILDER_BOARD_REFRESH_ZERO=1` reproduces the old value 0 and exists only to build the control network.
+- **Fresh networks:** Net-BR and Net-L04g (fixed builder) — the live Group A script gives **65/65** on each (the pre-fix twins gave 64/65 with this one failure). `A09-fix-genesis-diff.json`: their genesis differs from a pre-fix network of the same recipe in **exactly one slot**; the control Net-BR0 is **identical** to the pre-fix network. A14 (static scan + live block-0 state-root) re-applied to these three genesis files only: all pass, and Net-BR scanned *without* the added expectation fails with 1 deviation (the scan is sensitive to the slot).
+- **Behaviour on Net-BR (`Net-BR-board-refresh.json`, 21/21):** the getter equals the genesis timestamp (header, genesis.json, raw slot, alloc); 438 s after genesis 2,591,562 s of the 30 days remain; `refreshBoard()` is rejected with exactly `ValidatorsBoard: ordinary board changes are applied once every 30 days` — `eth_call` from a validator and from a non-validator, and **mined** (status 0, board state unchanged). **`syncBoard()` is not gated by the 30 days:** after a seated member (V5) requested exit it lost authority at once, `refreshBoard()` was *still rejected*, and `syncBoard()` removed V5 (4 members, `boardVersion` 2, one vacancy left because no outside candidate exists on a G5 network) without touching `lastBoardRefreshAt`; the exit left 4 validators and blocks kept coming.
+- **Negative control (Net-BR0, read-only):** value 0 → R1.2/R1.3/R1.4/R3.1/R4.1/R4.2 fail and `refreshBoard()` succeeds as an `eth_call` at once; the original Group A instrument reports exactly the A09 failure (64/65).
+- **Scope of the earlier genesis (`A09-fix-genesis-scope.json`):** all 36 genesis files scanned; **33 pre-fix networks** carry 0 (they are kept as evidence and were **not rebuilt**), 2 fixed, 1 control. The contract reads `lastBoardRefreshAt` in one function only (`refreshBoard()`); no earlier test script or raw result calls `refreshBoard()`, so no earlier PASS row depends on the value — inferred from the scripts that sent every transaction of the campaign, not from a chain-data scan. `syncBoard()`/`_fillVacancies()` do not read the field, so the earlier L02/L05 tests that used `syncBoard()` are unaffected.
+- **Not shown:** the 30-day boundary itself and the success path of `refreshBoard()` after 30 days (real time; the same non-testable item as before).
