+## 23. C-L04-6b: a re-added member that had already voted cannot vote again on the still-pending proposal — the message is `already voted`, not the eligibility message
+
+**Classification:** measurement (15/15, `Net-L04g-CL04-6b.json`). While M4 is removed its vote attempt gives `caller is not a member` (the `onlyMember` modifier runs before `_vote`); after the re-add (while the proposal is still pending and unexpired) the vote is rejected with `FoundationDAO: already voted` by `eth_call` and mined (status 0, votes unchanged, no double count); the proposal executes at exactly 8 distinct votes. Because `already voted` is checked before the membership and eligibility requirements, the message `not eligible - not a member when this proposal was created` cannot be produced for a member that already voted; for a re-added member that had **not** voted it was shown in C-L04-6 (S8.2). The first run on Net-BR (14/15) had a wrong expectation in my script (S3.3) and is kept as a SUPERSEDED row; see DEVIATIONS.md item 30.
